ps5: route the socket module through libSceNet.

A PS5 title's sandbox denies the raw BSD socket()/connect() syscalls (EACCES),
which made every outbound connection from Python add-ons fail. Sony's sceNet*
API is the permitted path (Kodi's curl uses it). Include ps5_pysocket.h in
socketmodule.c (guarded by -DPS5_PYSOCKET, cross build only), which #defines
socket/connect/send/recv/... to ps5_* wrappers over sceNet, defined in the
eboot. Scoped to this one file so Kodi, curl and libc are unaffected - a
process-wide --wrap of these names broke Kodi's own curl.
--- a/Modules/socketmodule.c
+++ b/Modules/socketmodule.c
@@ -262,6 +262,11 @@ shutdown(how) -- shut down traffic in one or both directions\n\
 /* Generic socket object definitions and includes */
 #define PySocket_BUILDING_SOCKET
 #include "socketmodule.h"
+#ifdef PS5_PYSOCKET
+/* Redirect this file's BSD socket calls to libSceNet (see ps5_pysocket.h).
+   Placed after all socket headers so it renames call sites, not declarations. */
+#include "ps5_pysocket.h"
+#endif
 
 /* Addressing includes */
 
